<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hvar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pharos</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hvar is a Croatian island in the central Adriatic. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> from Paros founded the colony of Pharos there in 384 BCE, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stari-grad">Stari Grad</a> Plain preserves their field divisions as a World Heritage Site. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> the island was held by the Narentines, Croatia-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and, from 1420 to 1797, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, under which Hvar town flourished as a naval base.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hvar.jpg" alt="Hvar" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard Gagnon · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_Hvar_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
